# Arrow keys walk EVERY card in a windowed digest list, not the built ones.
#
# The window builds sixteen of Blocked's eighty-one cards. The keyboard cursor
# is the one thing in this pane that must not agree with it: a person arrowing
# down a list has asked to reach the end of the list, and a cursor that walks
# only what is on screen stops dead at row sixteen with sixty-five rows below
# it and no way to say so.
#
# So render_digest keeps two passes: one over every matched row (which builds
# listRows_ and sums listY_, and is what the cursor and the scroll-into-view
# read) and one over the window (which builds cards). This pins that they have
# not been collapsed into one — the tempting simplification, and the one that
# reads correct because the screen looks right until you press Down seventeen
# times.
#
# It is also the half of the fix that no other assertion covers. The window's
# own test (digest_is_windowed.e2e) drives the mouse wheel, which moves the
# scroll offset directly; this drives the cursor, which moves the scroll offset
# only if the cursor knew where a row it never built was going to be.
#
# Twenty-five Downs takes the cursor ten rows past the bottom of the first
# window. Numbers are a function of the window height, which is why this pins
# one. Re-measure rather than nudge.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1180,"window_height":949,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_WIN_W=1180 HANABI_WIN_H=949 HANABI_STRESS_SESSIONS=300 HANABI_CARD_AUDIT=1 HANABI_VIEW=blocked

expect_text "Blocked on you"
expect_text "digest cards 16 of 81 @ 0"

key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 2
key DOWN
wait_frames 20

# The cursor is on row 25, which the first window never built, and the list
# came to it. A cursor that walked only the built cards stops at row 16 and
# this reads "@ 0" forever — the count above stays perfectly right while the
# bottom four fifths of the list are unreachable from the keyboard.
expect_text "digest cards 19 of 81 @ 10"
